@page "/"
@inject IConfiguration Config
@inject SealedLibraryService Library
@inject DocumentRegistry Registry

<PageTitle>Scenario 2 — Sealed Library</PageTitle>

<h1>Scenario 2 — SharePoint as the System of Record</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Documents live permanently in a <strong>sealed SharePoint library</strong>: no user or group
    holds any standing access — the only custodian is the app-only service principal. When a user
    clicks <strong>View/Edit</strong>, the app grants them permission on that one document
    (per their role in the application database), they edit as themselves in Word with autosave,
    co-authoring and Track Changes, and the grant is withdrawn automatically once the document
    goes idle and unlocked. In exchange: full version history with restore, real retention
    (recycle bin + Purview policy), and Microsoft's audit log on top of ours.
</p>

<h4>Demo flow</h4>
<ol>
    <li>Go to <a href="documents">Documents</a> and create a document — it is born in the sealed library with Track Changes enforced. Nobody can open it yet.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>View/Edit</strong> — watch the JIT grant appear in the <a href="access-db">Access Database</a>, then the document opens in Word.</li>
    <li>Browse the SharePoint site directly as a test user — only granted documents are visible; everything else is security-trimmed away, including search.</li>
    <li>Close Word — after the idle threshold the sweep withdraws the grant. The document vanishes from the user's SharePoint view.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Versions</strong> on any document — view history and restore any previous version as current.</li>
    <li>Run <strong>Reconcile</strong> on the Access Database page — proof that the app database is the single source of truth.</li>
</ol>

<h4>Setup status</h4>
<ul class="list-group" style="max-width: 720px">
    <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between">
        <span>Entra ID (AzureAd) configured — TenantId / ClientId / ClientSecret</span>
        @if (AadConfigured)
        {
            <span class="badge bg-success align-self-center">OK</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark align-self-center">Set in appsettings.json / user-secrets</span>
        }
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between">
        <span>Sealed library custodian (app-only Graph + DriveId)</span>
        @if (Library.IsConfigured)
        {
            <span class="badge bg-success align-self-center">OK</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark align-self-center">Required for Scenario 2</span>
        }
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between">
        <span>Registered documents in the app database</span>
        <span class="badge bg-secondary align-self-center">@Registry.Documents().Count</span>
    </li>
</ul>

<p class="mt-3 text-muted">
    See <code>README.md</code> for setup (redirect URI <code>https://localhost:7292/signin-oidc</code>).
    The application permission needs <code>Sites.Selected</code> with <em>write</em> granted on the target site.
</p>

@code {
    private bool AadConfigured =>
        !(Config["AzureAd:TenantId"] ?? "YOUR_").StartsWith("YOUR_") &&
        !(Config["AzureAd:ClientId"] ?? "YOUR_").StartsWith("YOUR_");
}
